    "rawOriginal": "# Scene 06 — Arrival Hall\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe Arrival Hall is the players' first glimpse of Whispering Reef Sanctuary.\n\nThis is not a dungeon entrance.\n\nIt is the moment the players realise they have discovered an ancient civilization.\n\nPause here.\n\nLet them absorb the scale before encouraging exploration.\n\n**Desired emotional transition**\n\n**Committed → Wonder**\n\n---\n\n# Original Purpose\n\nEvery visitor to Whispering Reef Sanctuary passed through this chamber.\n\nTravelling Sea Guardians arrived here after crossing the reef.\n\nMerfolk emissaries were welcomed here.\n\nPilgrims, scholars and messengers began their visit in this hall before being guided deeper into the sanctuary.\n\nThis was never a place of defence.\n\nIt was a place of welcome.\n\n---\n\n# Scene Setup\n\nAs the party emerges from the flooded passage, the sound of crashing waves disappears completely.\n\nOnly dripping water remains.\n\nAllow a few seconds of silence before reading the description.\n\n---\n\n# Read Aloud\n\nYou pull yourselves from the cold seawater onto smooth stone.\n\nThe air is cool but surprisingly fresh.\n\nBefore you stretches a vast natural cavern unlike anything you have ever seen.\n\nTowering columns of living coral rise from crystal-clear pools, merging seamlessly into the surrounding reef.\n\nSunlight pours through narrow shafts high above, scattering shimmering patterns across the floor like moving stars beneath the sea.\n\nGentle streams wind through carefully carved channels before disappearing into the depths of the sanctuary.\n\nNothing here feels conquered.\n\nNothing feels forced.\n\nIt is impossible to tell where nature ends...\n\nand where careful hands once began.\n\nFor a long moment...\n\nthe sanctuary says nothing.\n\nIt simply waits.\n\n---\n\n# What the Players Notice\n\nWithout making any checks:\n\n- The chamber is immense.\n- Living coral has been cultivated rather than left to grow wild.\n- Every water channel appears intentional.\n- There are no doors—only graceful stone archways.\n- The architecture feels organic, almost grown instead of built.\n- The sanctuary is remarkably intact despite its age.\n\n---\n\n# Exploration / Investigation\n\n## The Welcome Basin\n\nAt the centre of the hall lies a shallow circular basin fed by several tiny streams.\n\nThe water is perfectly clear.\n\nCharacters who touch it find it cool and exceptionally clean.\n\nThis basin once allowed weary travellers to wash away salt before entering the sanctuary.\n\n## Stone Relief\n\nOne wall depicts figures of many different peoples working together.\n\nHumans.\n\nSea elves.\n\nMerfolk.\n\nTritons.\n\nA goliath.\n\nNo figure stands above another.\n\nNo crowns.\n\nNo weapons.\n\nThe message is clear even without words.\n\nThis was an Order united by purpose, not blood.\n\n## Water Channels\n\nCharacters following the channels notice they all flow deeper into the sanctuary.\n\nWhatever lies ahead is literally the heart of this place.\n\n---\n\n# Atmosphere\n\n> **TODO — Campaign Horror System**\n\nChoose one subtle event.\n\nSuggestions:\n\n- A ray of sunlight shifts although no clouds pass overhead.\n- A distant splash echoes through the sanctuary.\n- One character briefly thinks they hear quiet chanting, but it is only flowing water.\n- Tiny fish dart through a channel before disappearing into darkness.\n\n---\n\n# Player Questions\n\n## \"Has this place really been abandoned for centuries?\"\n\nEverything suggests yes.\n\nNature has reclaimed much of the sanctuary.\n\nYet the craftsmanship remains unmistakable.\n\n## \"Can we identify the builders?\"\n\nNot yet.\n\nTheir identity remains a mystery.\n\nThe players only know that many peoples contributed.\n\n---\n\n# Running the Scene\n\nDo not rush into investigation.\n\nLet the players simply look.\n\nIf they begin discussing who built this place, the scene has succeeded.\n\nResist the temptation to explain anything.\n\nWonder is more valuable than answers.\n\n---\n\n# Thomas\n\nThomas slowly turns in place.\n\nHis voice is barely above a whisper.\n\n\"This...\n\n...this is beautiful.\"\n\nHe seems relieved.\n\nThe uneasy pull that brought him here has vanished.\n\nFor the first time since leaving Blacktide Haven, he is no longer looking toward the sea.\n\nHe is looking at the sanctuary.\n\n---\n\n# Transition\n\nSeveral natural passages lead deeper into the complex.\n\nThe broadest route follows the flowing water toward the Hall of Tides.\n\nContinue with **Scene 07 — Hall of Tides**.\n\n---\n\n# DM Notes\n\nThis is the visual identity of the Sea Guardians.\n\nEverything the players see from this point onward should reinforce three ideas:\n\n- Harmony with nature.\n- Quiet purpose.\n- A civilization that served rather than ruled.\n\nThis room should inspire awe, not fear.\n\nThe horror comes later.\n\n---\n\n# Future Callbacks\n\n- The relief establishes that the Sea Guardians were an Order composed of many peoples.\n- The flowing water foreshadows the importance of the Waterworks and Ritual Pool.\n- The architecture becomes the visual language of every future Sea Guardian sanctuary.\n",
