        "html": "<p>1. Agelus investigates resilient crops and reaches the Broken Atoll.\n2. He studies unusual old populations there.\n3. He writes Notebook 1.\n4. He leaves Notebook 1 and the seed chest with Tordeck.\n5. He travels north specifically to inspect the monastery&#x27;s reported Brineheart.\n6. He unexpectedly notices old Stormpea around former cultivated ground.\n7. This makes Tordeck&#x27;s stories about his tsunami-struck island relevant.\n8. Agelus later travels to Tordeck&#x27;s island.\n9. Stormpea distribution demonstrates that plants can preserve vanished land use.\n10. Agelus broadens his research.\n11. He eventually reaches Greenbank and the G region.\n12. Greenbank becomes a base for comparing old populations, modern stocks, provenance, and later trade.\n13. He rejects misleading indicators and reconstructs eight probable distribution centers.\n14. He chooses J as a strong test.\n15. He leaves his main research at Greenbank because he expects to return.\n16. He travels toward J.\n17. He reaches Sanctuary 2 and becomes stranded.\n18. The Company later reconstructs this journey without ever finding a Notebook 2.</p>",
